Turns off the fix of commit 44d7d12 (DESIGN.md §7.5: whenever the record
at a path is written, the want at that path is re-classified) where this
pin needs it, by restoring the pre-fix code: after a commit writes this
machine's own conflict-copy record, `FolderState::applied` no longer
re-classifies the want at the copy's path. A want for a peer's copy of the
same losing version then keeps fetching and lands over the node's own
record with a version that does not dominate it, which I8 reports.

test: delocal-sim regressions::a_want_for_a_peers_conflict_copy_meets_our_own_copy_as_a_merge
test: delocal-engine folder::tests::writing_our_own_conflict_copy_reclassifies_a_want_for_a_peers_copy

